License and Third-Party Notices
================================

This repository contains input files, selected output files, and processed data
from Quantum ESPRESSO calculations for monolayer MoS2.  It does not include the
Quantum ESPRESSO source code or executables.

Quantum ESPRESSO
----------------

Quantum ESPRESSO is free software released under the GNU General Public License.
Scientific work using Quantum ESPRESSO should acknowledge/cite the code.  The
recommended general references are:

- P. Giannozzi et al., J. Phys.: Condens. Matter 21, 395502 (2009).
- P. Giannozzi et al., J. Phys.: Condens. Matter 29, 465901 (2017).

Official Quantum ESPRESSO citation and license guidance:
https://www.quantum-espresso.org/Doc/user_guide/node6.html

Pseudopotentials
----------------

The included main pseudopotentials are PBE UPF files:

- mo_pbe_v1.uspp.F.UPF
- s_pbe_v1.4.uspp.F.UPF

The optical-response folder also includes norm-conserving ONCV
pseudopotentials:

- optical/Mo.nc.upf
- optical/S.nc.upf

The ONCV pseudopotential headers state that citation is not required under the
GNU GPL, but suggest citing:

- D. R. Hamann, Phys. Rev. B 88, 085117 (2013).

No ownership is claimed here over Quantum ESPRESSO or third-party
pseudopotentials; their original notices and licenses remain in effect.
